[522.115, "\u001b[H\u001b[2G\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 61 \u001b[22mpython3 scratch/bench_mm2.py                # transposed axpy form ~3x faster than best dot form\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 62 \u001b[22mpython3 scratch/bench_mm3.py                # unroll/tiling variants (tiling was slower)\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 63 \u001b[22mcd scratch && PYTHONPATH=.. python3 bench_unroll.py   # 2-row unroll best for layer mats, 4-row for classifier\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 64 \u001b[22mpython3 check.py -- python3 run.py\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 65 \u001b[22mpython3 check.py --tokens 64 --prompts 3 -- python3 run.py\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 66 \u001b[22mNUMBA_CACHE_DIR=$(mktemp -d) python3 - <<EOF \u001b[38;2;0;134;179m...\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m \u001b[38;2;0;134;179minspect_types\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m / \u001b[38;2;0;134;179minspect_llvm\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m \u001b[38;2;0;134;179m...\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m \u001b[38;2;0;134;179mEOF\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m   # \u001b[38;2;0;134;179mfloat32-only\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m, \u001b[38;2;0;134;179mno\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m \u001b[38;2;0;134;179mfast\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m \r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m    \u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;0;134;179mflags\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;"]
[522.115, "51m\u001b[2m 67 \u001b[22mpython3 scratch/speed.py                    # startup + tok/s\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 68 \u001b[22mpython3 scratch/edge.py                     # PIECE vs fixtures, empty prompt, max_new 0, FIXED, context stop\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 69 \u001b[22m```\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 70 \r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B 71 \u001b[22m`scratch/` holds only these benchmark and test helpers; `run.py` does not use them.\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 72 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 73 \u001b[22m## Limitations / choices to note\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 74 \u001b[22m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 75 \u001b[22m- **Summation order**: each matvec output is summed in the same order as run.c. Numba emits no\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 76 \u001b[22m  FMA here (no `contract` flag), while the build that produced the fixtures may have fused\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 77 \u001b[22m  multiply-adds. The differences are ~1e-5 in the logits.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 78 \u001b[22m- **Load-time transpose**: weights sit in memory once, in transposed form, plus an extra 98 MB\u001b["]
[522.117, "101G\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 79 \u001b[22m  transposed classifier copy because the classifier is shared with the embedding. Peak memory\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 80 \u001b[22m  during load is about 1 GB.\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 81 \u001b[22m- **Numba on-disk cache** (`cache=True`) writes compiled code to `__pycache__/` beside `run.py`.\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 82 \u001b[22m  Without it (e.g. a read-only dir with no fallback), the first start compiles for a few seconds.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 83 \u001b[22m  Before `READY`, a single warm-up forward runs and the KV cache is reset afterwards.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 84 \u001b[22m- **Unspecified edge cases**, handled as follows: an empty decoded piece prints `HEX ` (trailing\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 85 \u001b[22m  space, no bytes); FIXED/LOGITS with more than seq_len ids processes only the first seq_len;\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 86 \u001b[22m  `GENERATE 0 ...` answers `DONE 0 max` without a forward pass; if `max` and `context` happen on\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 87 \u001b[22m  the same token, `max` is reported; unknown commands "]
[522.117, "answer `ERR unknown command`. Token ids are\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 88 \u001b[22m  not range-checked (bounds checks are off in the kernels).\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 89 \u001b[22m- The tokenizer and protocol handling are plain Python (not compute); only the arithmetic is\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 90 \u001b[22m  compiled.\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 91 \u001b[22m- Throughput on this machine moved a lot between runs (roughly 62\u2013104 tok/s for the same command),\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;51;51;51m\u001b[2m 92 \u001b[22m  apparently from other load, so the speed figures above are rough.\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;175;175;175m\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\u254c\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m Do you want to create \u001b[1mNOTES.md\u001b[22m?\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;87;105;247m\u276f\u001b[4G\u001b[38;2;102;102;102m1"]
[522.118, ". \u001b[38;2;87;105;247mYes\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;102;102;102m2. \u001b[39mYes, and switch to \u001b[1maccept edits (auto-approve file edits and common file commands)\u001b[22m for this session \u001b[1m(shift+tab)\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;102;102;102m3. \u001b[39mNo\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;102;102;102mEsc to cancel \u00b7 Tab\u001b[22Gto amend\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[40;1H\u001b[36;2H"]
